"`qrmi_config.json`, not in this file.\n"
msgstr "Hindi na kailangang baguhin ang `[qrmi]` table, dahil ang `qrmi-runtime` block ang nagbibigay ng instance at ng QPU. Itakda lang ang `resource` para i-override ang Backend. Nananatili ang mga credential sa `qrmi_config.json`, hindi sa file na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `slurm` profile holds the scheduler and resource settings of a generic Slurm cluster, and\n"
"any key in your file overrides it. The commented `[sqd_advanced]` table sets the\n"
"`sqd-advanced-settings` block, the commented `[advanced]` table sets block names and timeouts,\n"
"and the table of each solver holds its tuning. To choose the nodes, ranks, and threads of the solver jobs, see\n"
"[Size the SQD diagonalization for your HPC resources](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qcsc-prefect/tutorials/configure_sqd_solver_resources/).\n"
msgstr "Hawak ng `slurm` profile ang mga setting ng scheduler at resource ng isang generic na Slurm cluster, at ino-override ito ng anumang key sa file mo. Itinatakda ng naka-comment na `[sqd_advanced]` table ang `sqd-advanced-settings` block, itinatakda ng naka-comment na `[advanced]` table ang mga pangalan ng block at timeout, at hawak ng table ng bawat solver ang tuning nito. Para piliin ang mga node, rank, at thread ng mga solver job, tingnan ang [Size the SQD diagonalization for your HPC resources](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qcsc-prefect/tutorials/configure_sqd_solver_resources/).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
