# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pag-execute sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Optimize stage, the task `get_lucj_params` in the workflow, fits the ansatz to the QPU before any circuit exists. ffsim builds the LUCJ operator from $t_2$ with only the interactions that a heavy-hex lattice runs without SWAP gates. These are the same-spin pairs of neighboring orbitals and the opposite-spin pairs on every fourth orbital, at most five on a heavy-hex (Heron) processor. ffsim then compresses the operator (`optimize=True`, on by default in the workflow) so that one layer reproduces $t_2$ more closely.\n"
msgstr "Ang Optimize stage, ang task na `get_lucj_params` sa workflow, ay iniaangkop ang ansatz sa QPU bago pa magkaroon ng anumang Circuit. Binubuo ng ffsim ang LUCJ operator mula sa $t_2$ na may mga interaction lang na tinatakbo ng heavy-hex lattice nang walang SWAP Gate. Ito ang mga same-spin na pares ng magkatabing orbital at ang mga opposite-spin na pares sa bawat ikaapat na orbital, hanggang lima sa isang heavy-hex (Heron) na processor. Pagkatapos ay kino-compress ng ffsim ang operator (`optimize=True`, naka-on bilang default sa workflow) para mas malapit na ma-reproduce ng isang layer ang $t_2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Trace:** The task `get_lucj_params` has the tag `optimize`. Its result carries everything that the circuit needs, so one arrow leads from it to `quantum_sampling`.\n"
msgstr "**Trace:** May tag na `optimize` ang task na `get_lucj_params`. Dala ng resulta nito ang lahat ng kailangan ng Circuit, kaya isang arrow ang papunta mula rito sa `quantum_sampling`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Configure:** The **Circuit** group of the run form sets the LUCJ layers, the compression and its iteration limit, and the **QPU Topology** (`heavy-hex` or `square`), which sets the interaction pairs. The `sqd-advanced-settings` block holds reset mitigation and the transpiler settings (the optimization level and the SABRE layout search) that the Execute stage uses.\n"
msgstr "**Configure:** Itinatakda ng **Circuit** group ng run form ang mga LUCJ layer, ang compression at ang iteration limit nito, at ang **QPU Topology** (`heavy-hex` o `square`), na nagtatakda ng mga interaction pair. Hawak ng `sqd-advanced-settings` block ang reset mitigation at ang mga setting ng Transpiler (ang optimization level at ang SABRE layout search) na ginagamit ng Execute stage.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Resume:** The result is persisted (`compressed/pickle`), so a long compression runs only one time, even if you retry the run.\n"
msgstr "**Resume:** Naka-persist ang resulta (`compressed/pickle`), kaya isang beses lang tatakbo ang mahabang compression, kahit i-retry mo ang run.\n"

