# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retry a failed run, and reuse its samples {#retry-a-failed-run-and-reuse-its-samples}"
msgstr "I-retry ang bigong run, at gamitin muli ang mga sample nito {#retry-a-failed-run-and-reuse-its-samples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Retry:** Suppose that, in a run with **Max Iteration** set to `10`, a solver job hits its walltime in round 5 and `sqd_loop` fails. Raise the walltime in the `exec-sqd-fulqrum-slurm` block under **Blocks**, then select **Retry** on the failed flow run. The retried run loads the stored results of the first three stages and submits no QPU job. It runs only `sqd_loop` again, with the new walltime, and starts at round 5 from the checkpoint of round 4. Its log shows `[ckpt] RESUME from …: completed 4 step(s)`, then `SQD iteration 5/10`, as in the following image.\n"
msgstr "**Retry:** Ipagpalagay na, sa isang run na may **Max Iteration** na naka-set sa `10`, umabot sa walltime ang isang solver job sa round 5 at pumalya ang `sqd_loop`. Taasan ang walltime sa `exec-sqd-fulqrum-slurm` block sa ilalim ng **Blocks**, pagkatapos piliin ang **Retry** sa bigong flow run. Nilo-load ng na-retry na run ang mga nakaimbak na resulta ng unang tatlong stage at walang isinusumiteng QPU job. Ang `sqd_loop` lang ang pinapatakbo nitong muli, gamit ang bagong walltime, at nagsisimula sa round 5 mula sa checkpoint ng round 4. Ipinapakita ng log nito ang `[ckpt] RESUME from …: completed 4 step(s)`, pagkatapos ang `SQD iteration 5/10`, tulad sa sumusunod na larawan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Reuse:** A new run computes everything again unless you point it to earlier samples. To try another subspace dimension with the same samples, start a custom run with the same parameters, set **Load from QRMI Job Directory** (`qrmi_result_dir`) to the work directory in the `sqd-sampling-source` artifact of the first run, and change **Subspace Dimension**. The new run replaces `get_lucj_params` and `quantum_sampling` with `load_qrmi_result`, which reads the samples and submits nothing to the QPU. **Reset Mitigation** in `sqd-advanced-settings` must match the first run, because the reload applies it. For samples taken through IQP, set **Load from Qiskit Runtime Job ID** (`qiskit_runtime_job_id`) instead, and the stage is `load_runtime_job`. It reads the job with the credentials of the prefect-qiskit `QuantumRuntime` block named in **Quantum Runtime Block (reload)** (`ibm-runner` by default). Create that block one time with `prefect block create quantum-runtime`.\n"
msgstr "**Reuse:** Kinukwenta muli ng bagong run ang lahat maliban kung ituturo mo ito sa mga naunang sample. Para subukan ang ibang subspace dimension gamit ang parehong mga sample, magsimula ng custom run na may parehong mga parameter, itakda ang **Load from QRMI Job Directory** (`qrmi_result_dir`) sa work directory sa `sqd-sampling-source` artifact ng unang run, at baguhin ang **Subspace Dimension**. Pinapalitan ng bagong run ang `get_lucj_params` at `quantum_sampling` ng `load_qrmi_result`, na nagbabasa ng mga sample at walang isinusumite sa QPU. Dapat tumugma ang **Reset Mitigation** sa `sqd-advanced-settings` sa unang run, dahil ina-apply ito ng reload. Para sa mga sample na kinuha sa pamamagitan ng IQP, itakda na lang ang **Load from Qiskit Runtime Job ID** (`qiskit_runtime_job_id`), at ang stage ay `load_runtime_job`. Binabasa nito ang job gamit ang mga credential ng prefect-qiskit `QuantumRuntime` block na pinangalanan sa **Quantum Runtime Block (reload)** (`ibm-runner` bilang default). Gawin ang block na iyon nang isang beses gamit ang `prefect block create quantum-runtime`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Continue a recovery with more rounds:** Start a custom run with the same parameters, set **Resume from Checkpoint** (`resume_checkpoint`) to the path in the `sqd-checkpoint` artifact of the first run, and raise **Max Iteration**. The new run continues after the completed rounds, from the stored occupancies and best energy. For example, a checkpoint with 32 of 100 rounds done and **Max Iteration** set to `200` continues at round 33/200. The new run reads that checkpoint and writes its own, and the following rules apply.\n"
msgstr "**Ipagpatuloy ang recovery nang mas maraming round:** Magsimula ng custom run na may parehong mga parameter, itakda ang **Resume from Checkpoint** (`resume_checkpoint`) sa path sa `sqd-checkpoint` artifact ng unang run, at taasan ang **Max Iteration**. Tumutuloy ang bagong run pagkatapos ng mga nakumpletong round, mula sa mga nakaimbak na occupancy at pinakamahusay na enerhiya. Halimbawa, ang checkpoint na may 32 sa 100 round na tapos at **Max Iteration** na naka-set sa `200` ay tutuloy sa round 33/200. Binabasa ng bagong run ang checkpoint na iyon at isinusulat ang sarili nitong checkpoint, at nalalapat ang mga sumusunod na patakaran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The samples, the molecule, **Subspace Dimension**, **Batch Number**, and the solver type (the `fulqrum_solver_job` part of the solver block) must match the first run, so reuse its samples as in **Reuse**.\n"
msgstr "Dapat tumugma sa unang run ang mga sample, ang molecule, **Subspace Dimension**, **Batch Number**, at ang uri ng solver (ang bahaging `fulqrum_solver_job` ng solver block), kaya gamitin muli ang mga sample nito tulad sa **Reuse**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The name and the job settings of the solver block, such as its walltime, can change.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring magbago ang pangalan at ang mga job setting ng solver block, tulad ng walltime nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a setting that must match differs, the run fails before any solver job and names the difference.\n"
msgstr "Kung iba ang isang setting na dapat tumugma, pumapalya ang run bago ang anumang solver job at pinangangalanan ang pagkakaiba.\n"

